            "id": "14011927",
            "headline": "Appliance maker Atomberg files draft IPO papers with Rs 450-crore fresh issue",
            "heading": "Appliance maker Atomberg files draft IPO papers with Rs 450-crore fresh issue",
            "intro": "Among the investors paring their stakes through the offer for sale are A91 Emerging Fund I LLP, V-Sciences Investments, Jungle Ventures IV and Inflexor Opportunities Fund 1.",
            "body": "Consumer appliances maker Atomberg Technologies has filed draft papers for an initial public offering, comprising a fresh issue of shares worth up to Rs 450 crore and an offer for sale of up to 76.5 million shares by existing investors, according to documents filed on Friday. The company did not disclose the overall size of the issue.\r\n\r\nAmong the investors paring their stakes through the offer for sale are A91 Emerging Fund I LLP, V-Sciences Investments, Jungle Ventures IV and Inflexor Opportunities Fund 1.\r\n\r\nThe Mumbai-based company plans to deploy Rs 340 crore of the fresh proceeds towards repaying debt, funding brand-building initiatives and investing in research and development.\r\n\r\nAtomberg makes a range of consumer appliances including fans, smart locks, water purifiers and cold-pressed juicers. It also manufactures and supplies motor and electronics components to enterprise customers such as Voltas, Godrej and Blue Star, giving it a foothold on both the consumer and business-to-business sides of the appliances market.\r\n\r\nThe company's revenue from operations climbed to Rs 1,294 crore in the fiscal year ended March 2026, up from Rs 797 crore in fiscal 2024 \u2014 growth of about 62% over two years.\r\n\r\nAtomberg is positioning itself against the backdrop of a shifting appliances market. India's consumer appliances sector was estimated at $4.69 billion in fiscal 2026, according to the draft papers, and the company argues demand is tilting towards next-generation, energy-efficient products. Rising incomes, urbanisation and premiumisation are driving purchases of fans, water purifiers and motorised kitchen appliances, it said.\r\n\r\nAs of March 31, 2026, the company operated through 626 distributors and direct dealers, nearly 47,000 retail touchpoints, and a service network spanning more than 18,000 pin codes across India.",
