          "2": {
            "id": "14011872",
            "headline": "Lumino Industries IPO to hit Dalal Street on August 27; issue size trimmed",
            "heading": "Lumino Industries IPO to hit Dalal Street on August 27; issue size trimmed",
            "intro": "Lumino Industries IPO | The company is expected to finalise the IPO share allotment by September 1, while trading in its equity shares is expected to commence on the stock exchanges on September 3.",
            "body": "Kolkata-based conductor, power cable and electrical wire manufacturer Lumino Industries has finalised plans to launch its Rs 700-crore IPO for public subscription on August 27, according to the red herring prospectus filed with the Registrar of Companies on Thursday.\r\n\r\nThe company aims to raise Rs 500 crore through a fresh issue of equity shares, while promoters Devendra Goel and his son Jay Goel will sell shares worth up to Rs 200 crore through an offer for sale (OFS).\r\n\r\nLumino had initially proposed to raise Rs 1,000 crore through an initial share sale comprising a fresh issue of Rs 600 crore and an OFS of Rs 400 crore, according to the draft red herring prospectus filed with SEBI and the stock exchanges in January 2025. The IPO proposal was subsequently approved by the capital markets regulator in June 2025.\r\n\r\nThe one-day anchor book will open for institutional investors on August 25, while the issue will close for public subscription on August 31.\r\n\r\nLumino Industries is expected to finalise the IPO share allotment by September 1, while trading in its equity shares is expected to commence on the stock exchanges on September 3.\r\n\r\nThe company will finalise the price band separately on August 21.\r\n\r\nThe company supplies conductors, power cables and other specialised products to large EPC players such as Kalpataru Projects International, Jackson, Warora Kurnool Transmission, K G N Electricals, WRSS XXI (A) Transco, Monte Carlo and R S Infraprojects. It also offers its products to international clients in countries including the United States, Mali, Burkina Faso, Nepal, Bangladesh, Kenya, Ghana, Rwanda and Ethiopia.\r\n\r\nClick Here To Read All IPO News\r\n\r\nDomestic business contributed 98 percent of its topline in FY26, while the remaining portion of revenue came from exports. The company had an aggregate order book of Rs 3,149.8 crore as of the end of the year.\r\n\r\nLumino Industries will utilise Rs 337 crore of the net proceeds from the fresh issue to repay debt, against total outstanding borrowings of Rs 1,856.7 crore as of July 2026.\r\n\r\nFurther, Rs 15 crore will be spent on the purchase of equipment and machinery, civil works and interior development at its existing manufacturing facility. The remaining funds will be used for general corporate purposes.\r\n\r\nThe company has reserved up to Rs 10 crore worth of equity shares for its employees. Half of the net issue size, excluding the employee allocation, has been reserved for qualified institutional buyers, while 35 percent of the shares have been set aside for retail investors and the remaining 15 percent for non-institutional investors.\r\n\r\nOn the financial front, Lumino Industries, a power EPC company that counts listed players such as Apar Industries, Bajel Projects, Kalpataru Projects International, KEC International, KEI Industries and Universal Cables among its peers, reported a profit of Rs 160 crore for the fiscal year ended March 2026, an increase of 28.4 percent from Rs 124.6 crore in the previous year. Revenue during the same period rose 6.4 percent to Rs 2,041 crore from Rs 1,918 crore.\r\n\r\nMotilal Oswal Investment Advisors, JM Financial and Monarch Networth Capital have been appointed as the merchant bankers to manage the Lumino Industries IPO.",
